    "done_when": "tests/test_lane_reading_carries_counts.py gains a case where the document names its generating count under the alias the dispatch code accepts (currently _GENERATING_KEYS near dispatch.py:2603, including running), asserting the payload's lane_reading carries that count; a second case asserts lane_document.py's reader, called directly, returns the same counts the payload carries for the file's existing fixtures. git grep of the lane-document key names (generating, waiting, running) in reckon/crew/dispatch.py at the head returns no read of the document's raw keys outside a call into lane_document.py, recorded in the manifest. The alias case fails at the base revision if the alias is untested there, or else the manifest states it passes at base with the reason. The negative control, in a scratch copy, drops the alias from the lane-document reader; the alias case fails, with the mutation on the red log's first line and an EXIT= line after pytest's output. The gate is tests/test_lane_reading_carries_counts.py, tests/test_lane_document.py plus the existing lane_reading test files; both arms are recorded as one JSON object each under baseline_suite and after_suite (revision, command, exit_status, one log_path, failure_ids), each log ending in an EXIT= line, with the head arm adding no failing id. ruff check plus ruff format --check on the changed paths add no finding against the base. The tests neither read nor write the real lane document or ~/.config/reckon.",
